# How to cite this package. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo uses it for the DOI of each release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "golemcat: Computerized Adaptive Testing of the Big Five with the Rating Scale Model"
abstract: "A 'shiny' application, built as a 'golem' package, that gives the 50 statements of the IPIP Big-Five Factor Markers as a computerized adaptive test (CAT). Each trait is scored with the rating scale model, the next statement is the one with the most Fisher information at the current expected a posteriori (EAP) estimate, and a trait stops when its standard error reaches a threshold. The app is the questionnaire as a respondent sees it, with a profile of the five traits at the end and a PDF report of it, made with 'typst'. The engine, which gives the same results as 'catR', and the session logic are also R functions, and any item bank fitted with the rating scale model of 'mirt' can be read."
authors:
